{"title":"Heptagon","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>heptagon</b> is a polygon with seven sides. The sum of the interior angles of a heptagon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/1/031b02033a54ab2416c6f749dfc540efd7ceb945.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$900^{\\circ}.$\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" /> Therefore, the measure on an interior angle in a regular heptagon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/d/6adb4ee073c02f977a9dcbe0d4d059fefd5ed259.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{900}7^{\\circ}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"42\" height=\"38\" /> A heptagon will have 14 diagnols and can be split into 5 triangles. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Heptagon&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polygon\" title=\"Polygon\">Polygon</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometry\" title=\"Geometry\">Geometry</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Heptagon&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018090228\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.008 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.013 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 19/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 265/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 345/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.459     